# `build/` is covered by the repo root's .gitignore; these are not. The glob on
# twister-out catches the numbered backups twister makes on a re-run
# (twister-out.1, .2, ...), not just the current one.
#
# All three hold symlinks into ~/zephyrproject, which is why the root `fmt-c`
# task takes its file list from `git ls-files` rather than from a `**` glob: a
# glob that followed them would reformat the Zephyr installation in place.
build_test/
twister-out*/
